WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.506 --> 00:00:03.442
primarily with the tempemptations.

00:00:03.575 --> 00:00:04.643
My heartfelt condolences go out

00:00:04.776 --> 00:00:06.511
to his family and friends.

00:00:06.645 --> 00:00:07.112
&gt;&gt; Absolutely.

00:00:07.245 --> 00:00:08.046
&gt;&gt;&gt; Also this morning, the

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.148
company that owns Madison square

00:00:10.482 --> 00:00:11.983
garden, radio city music hall

00:00:12.117 --> 00:00:13.718
and other famous New York venues

00:00:13.852 --> 00:00:15.454
says that all lawyers who work

00:00:15.587 --> 00:00:17.456
at firms representing a client

00:00:17.589 --> 00:00:20.125
suing them are banned.

00:00:20.492 --> 00:00:22.694
Msg entertainment is denying

00:00:22.828 --> 00:00:24.095
entry to anyone on its exclusion

00:00:24.496 --> 00:00:26.565
list, from attending concerts or

00:00:26.698 --> 00:00:27.532
sporting events.

00:00:27.666 --> 00:00:29.568
Here's what's a key part of

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:29.868
this.

00:00:30.001 --> 00:00:30.602
They are using facial

00:00:30.735 --> 00:00:32.137
recognition technology to do it.

00:00:32.504 --> 00:00:33.672
CNN's Omar Jiminez is covering

00:00:33.805 --> 00:00:34.506
this story.

00:00:34.639 --> 00:00:36.508
This is remarkable.

00:00:36.508 --> 00:00:37.142
"A," because of the facial

00:00:37.275 --> 00:00:38.610
recognition aspect, but "B,"

00:00:38.743 --> 00:00:39.778
it's not just the attorneys who

00:00:39.911 --> 00:00:41.079
are involved in the suing.

00:00:41.213 --> 00:00:42.514
It's any attorneys that work at

00:00:42.514 --> 00:00:43.048
firms that are representing

00:00:43.181 --> 00:00:44.549
those who are suing these

00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:44.883
venues.

00:00:45.016 --> 00:00:45.951
&gt;&gt; And I think that was the

00:00:46.084 --> 00:00:47.219
surprise for a lot of people.

00:00:47.352 --> 00:00:48.920
It's like, I'm not even involved

00:00:49.054 --> 00:00:50.522
in the litigation of this, and

00:00:50.522 --> 00:00:51.990
all of a sudden, I am banned, at

00:00:52.123 --> 00:00:53.124
least temporarily as well.

00:00:53.258 --> 00:00:55.126
And it's part of what New York

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.728
attorney general Letitia James

00:00:56.862 --> 00:00:58.029
is concerned about here.

00:00:58.163 --> 00:00:59.130
Not just potentially dissuading

00:00:59.264 --> 00:01:01.933
those from holding Madison

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:02.601
square garden entertainment

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:04.736
potentially accountable, but

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:05.871
also the technology involved

00:01:06.004 --> 00:01:07.138
with it.

00:01:07.272 --> 00:01:08.840
Msg maintains that they are

00:01:08.974 --> 00:01:13.545
fully within their rights.

00:01:13.678 --> 00:01:15.113
&gt;&gt; Come up on matching somebody

00:01:15.247 --> 00:01:16.581
on a facial recognition list.

00:01:16.715 --> 00:01:19.284
&gt;&gt; He was recognized on facial

00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:21.520
recognition cameras, then

00:01:21.653 --> 00:01:21.920
confronted.

00:01:22.053 --> 00:01:25.023
&gt;&gt; Are you Benjamin norry?

00:01:25.156 --> 00:01:25.357
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:31.029
&gt;&gt; This is how lawyer Benjamin

00:01:31.162 --> 00:01:31.763
Norman was greeted.

00:01:31.897 --> 00:01:33.031
&gt;&gt; The ticket has been revoked

00:01:33.164 --> 00:01:34.566
and you are not permitted in the

00:01:34.633 --> 00:01:35.033
building.

00:01:35.166 --> 00:01:36.868
&gt;&gt; It's because norren works for

00:01:37.002 --> 00:01:38.169
a law firm representing ticket

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.139
brokers in a lawsuit against

00:01:41.273 --> 00:01:42.574
Madison square garden

00:01:42.574 --> 00:01:42.841
entertainment.

00:01:42.974 --> 00:01:44.175
All of the roughly 60 lawyers at

00:01:44.576 --> 00:01:45.944
his firm are also banned until

00:01:46.077 --> 00:01:47.445
the litigation is resolved.

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:52.584
&gt;&gt; We received a letter from msg

00:01:52.584 --> 00:01:54.586
stating that because of this

00:01:54.586 --> 00:01:56.721
litigation, all attorneys in our

00:01:56.855 --> 00:01:57.956
firm, even those attorneys who

00:01:58.089 --> 00:01:58.890
have nothing to do whatsoever

00:01:59.024 --> 00:02:00.125
with the litigation, will be

00:02:00.258 --> 00:02:01.993
barred for the duration of the

00:02:02.127 --> 00:02:02.594
litigation.

00:02:02.594 --> 00:02:04.129
&gt;&gt; Reporter: The firm's

00:02:04.262 --> 00:02:05.063
co-founding partner has been a

00:02:05.196 --> 00:02:07.198
season ticket holder for 47

00:02:07.332 --> 00:02:07.499
years.

00:02:07.632 --> 00:02:09.568
He believes here, he's being

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:11.903
retaliated against.

00:02:12.037 --> 00:02:14.606
&gt;&gt; The focus of their ban is to

00:02:14.706 --> 00:02:16.608
dissuade people from suing

00:02:16.608 --> 00:02:17.809
Madison square garden.

00:02:17.943 --> 00:02:20.145
If you have to think about, do I

00:02:20.278 --> 00:02:22.614
have a choice of being banned

00:02:22.747 --> 00:02:23.682
and representing somebody,

00:02:23.815 --> 00:02:25.183
somebody is going to say, I

00:02:25.317 --> 00:02:26.618
don't need that aggravation.

00:02:26.651 --> 00:02:28.853
I'm not going to take that.

00:02:28.987 --> 00:02:30.755
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Their firm is among

00:02:30.889 --> 00:02:32.290
dozens temporarily banned from

00:02:32.624 --> 00:02:34.793
msg properties, including radio

00:02:34.926 --> 00:02:36.061
city music hall, while they

00:02:36.194 --> 00:02:38.630
represent clients suing the

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:38.697
garden.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:40.231
New York attorney general

00:02:40.632 --> 00:02:41.199
Letitia James believes they may

00:02:41.333 --> 00:02:42.667
be violating state and city

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:44.669
laws, writing to them in part,

00:02:44.803 --> 00:02:45.637
forbidding entry to lawyers

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:47.105
representing clients who have

00:02:47.238 --> 00:02:48.640
engaged in litigation against a

00:02:48.673 --> 00:02:49.975
company may dissuade such

00:02:50.108 --> 00:02:51.042
lawyers from taking on

00:02:51.176 --> 00:02:52.243
legitimate cases.

00:02:52.644 --> 00:02:54.179
Days later, Madison square

00:02:54.312 --> 00:02:59.451
garden emphasized it's a private

00:02:59.584 --> 00:03:01.853
business and in compliance with

00:03:01.987 --> 00:03:03.288
all laws, writing in part, the

00:03:03.421 --> 00:03:06.658
attorneys prohibited from

00:03:06.658 --> 00:03:07.492
attending includes money

00:03:07.626 --> 00:03:08.727
grabbers who capitalize on the

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:09.628
misfortune of others.

00:03:09.761 --> 00:03:10.829
This includes attorneys

00:03:10.962 --> 00:03:12.664
representing ticket scalpers,

00:03:12.797 --> 00:03:14.065
personal injury claims, and

00:03:14.199 --> 00:03:15.400
class action litigations, but

00:03:15.533 --> 00:03:18.103
does not include claims related

00:03:18.236 --> 00:03:19.371
to sexual harassment or

00:03:19.504 --> 00:03:20.071
employment discrimination.

00:03:20.205 --> 00:03:22.107
&gt;&gt; You get to say who you serve.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:23.308
And if it's somebody who is

00:03:23.441 --> 00:03:25.076
suing you and trying to put you

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.177
out of business or take your

00:03:26.311 --> 00:03:27.979
money from you, right, et

00:03:28.113 --> 00:03:31.049
cetera, you have a right to be,

00:03:31.182 --> 00:03:32.684
yes, a little unhappy about it.

00:03:32.784 --> 00:03:34.886
&gt;&gt; You know, it doesn't seem

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:35.920
like they're letting up.

00:03:36.054 --> 00:03:37.188
If anything, they've been

00:03:37.322 --> 00:03:37.722
doubling down.

00:03:37.856 --> 00:03:39.924
&gt;&gt; No, no, tripling down, even.

00:03:40.058 --> 00:03:41.626
&gt;&gt; Some experts believe it's a

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.428
slippery slope and not just the

00:03:43.561 --> 00:03:44.696
discretionary power of who else

00:03:44.829 --> 00:03:46.998
could be flagged in the future,

00:03:47.132 --> 00:03:48.700
but one method being used to

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:49.467
enforce it.

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:50.702
Even if it is legal.

00:03:50.769 --> 00:03:53.104
&gt;&gt; I have read their privacy

00:03:53.238 --> 00:03:53.438
policy.

00:03:53.571 --> 00:03:55.340
They explicitly say that the

00:03:55.473 --> 00:03:56.141
biometrics that they capture

00:03:56.274 --> 00:03:59.077
from you can be used for any

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.812
purpose that would benefit their

00:04:00.945 --> 00:04:01.846
economic interest.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:03.982
There's all sorts of things they

00:04:04.115 --> 00:04:05.583
could be doing with face

00:04:05.717 --> 00:04:07.819
recognition, and there's so much

00:04:07.952 --> 00:04:08.920
minimal transparency around it,

00:04:09.054 --> 00:04:10.055
because they're a private

00:04:10.188 --> 00:04:10.388
company.

00:04:10.722 --> 00:04:11.489
&gt;&gt; Some don't believe it should

00:04:11.623 --> 00:04:12.724
be used at all.

00:04:12.724 --> 00:04:14.726
&gt;&gt; It's so primed to be misused.

00:04:14.726 --> 00:04:15.994
It's so prone to discrimination.

00:04:16.127 --> 00:04:18.730
And I am terrified of the day

00:04:18.763 --> 00:04:20.365
where we allow companies to use

00:04:20.732 --> 00:04:23.334
so many forms of tracking and

00:04:23.468 --> 00:04:24.736
surveillance that, you know, we

00:04:24.736 --> 00:04:26.738
end up in the middle of one of

00:04:26.771 --> 00:04:28.740
the largest cities on the planet

00:04:28.807 --> 00:04:29.474
without any place we can

00:04:29.607 --> 00:04:32.177
actually go, while keeping our

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:32.744
privacy.

00:04:32.744 --> 00:04:33.945
&gt;&gt; Now, Madison square garden

00:04:34.079 --> 00:04:35.280
says they've been using facial

00:04:35.413 --> 00:04:37.682
recognition to help create a

00:04:37.816 --> 00:04:38.817
safe environment since 2018.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:40.018
But there are a lot of factors

00:04:40.151 --> 00:04:42.053
here that people are concerned

00:04:42.187 --> 00:04:42.754
about.

00:04:42.821 --> 00:04:44.389
They've gone until February 13th

00:04:44.756 --> 00:04:46.224
to respond to attorney general

00:04:46.357 --> 00:04:47.392
James' inquiries.

00:04:47.525 --> 00:04:48.760
Obviously, though, still an

00:04:48.827 --> 00:04:49.461
ongoing battle here.

